## tags: superstition
Fan death | 선풍기 사망 | 4 | | seonpunggi samang, ~sleeping with a fan on | The belief that a fan running overnight in a closed room can kill.
Number four | 숫자 4 | 4 | | four, 4, sa, ~unlucky four | 4 (sa) sounds like "death"; many buildings skip the 4th floor.
Writing names in red | 빨간 이름 | 4 | | red ink, red pen, writing name in red | Red ink is for the names of the dead.
Whistling at night | 밤에 휘파람 | 3 | | whistling at night, ~whistle at night | Calls snakes or ghosts, so don't.
Shaking your leg | 다리 떨기 | 3 | | leg shaking, ~shaking legs | Shakes your luck (or wealth) away.
Pig dream | 돼지꿈 | 3 | | dwaeji kkum, ~dreaming of pigs | A lucky dream: buy a lottery ticket.
Taemong | 태몽 | 3 | | ~conception dream | A dream foretelling a pregnancy and the child's nature.
Seaweed soup before exams | 시험 전 미역국 | 3 | | miyeokguk before exams, ~seaweed soup before an exam | Slippery seaweed makes you "slip" (fail).
Yeot before exams | 시험 전 엿 | 2 | | yeot for exams, ~sticky taffy for exams | Sticky taffy helps answers stick.
Shoes as a gift | 신발 선물 | 2 | | giving shoes, ~gifting shoes to a lover | A partner given shoes will run away.
Cutting nails at night | 밤에 손톱 깎기 | 2 | | ~clipping nails at night | Mice eat the clippings and turn into you.
Stepping on the threshold | 문지방 밟기 | 2 | | munjibang, ~stepping on a doorsill | Brings bad luck.
Magpie means guests | 까치 손님 | 2 | | kkachi, ~magpie brings guests | A magpie's call means visitors or good news.
Samjae | 삼재 | 2 | | ~three calamities | A recurring three-year period of misfortune.
Son eomneun nal | 손 없는 날 | 2 | | son eopneun nal, ~day without spirits | Wandering-spirit-free days, prized for moving house.
Poop dream | 똥꿈 | 2 | | ttong kkum, ~dreaming of poop | Weirdly, a sign of money coming.
Dead person in a dream | 조상꿈 | 1 | | josang kkum, ~ancestor dream | Ancestors in dreams bring messages or luck.
Tteok after moving | 이사떡 | 2 | | isa tteok, ~moving rice cakes | Sharing red-bean rice cakes to keep misfortune away from the new house.

